// @test: run
// @level: L1
// @tier: 0
// @tags: term, render, cell, const, visibility, regression
// @timeout: 120000
// @expected-stdout-begin
// empty skip=false width=1 grapheme=[ ]
// empty style fg=false bg=false
// default style fg=false bg=false
// distinct eq_self=true eq_other=false
// @expected-stdout-end
// @description: A public associated constant declared on a stdlib type is
//   reachable from a user program, and carries the record its declaration
//   names.
//
// WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `RenderCell.EMPTY` (core/term/render/cell.vr:27) is
// a `public const` and was reachable on a binary built 2026-08-31 — that
// binary ran this exact expression and printed `skip=false grapheme=[ ]`.
// On 2026-09-09 the same source answered
//
//   error<E404>: field 'EMPTY' not found on type 'RenderCell'.
//   Available members: [eq, grapheme, reset, set_char, skip, style, width]
//
// The constant had not moved; the archive had. Writing the precompiled
// stdlib runs a visibility-demotion pass that asks, of a BARE LEAF name,
// "is this name private somewhere and public nowhere?" — and the walk that
// answered the public half could see only TOP-LEVEL declarations. A private
// top-level `const EMPTY` in core/collections/map.vr therefore put "EMPTY"
// into the private set, the public `RenderCell.EMPTY` could not put it into
// the public set because it is an ASSOCIATED constant, and the descriptor
// was stamped private on its way into the archive. One name, measured: of
// 55 core types declaring a public associated const, exactly one differed
// between the two binaries. See T1306.
//
// WHY EACH LINE. A spec that only asserted "this compiles" would pass on a
// constant that resolved to nothing, which is the failure mode next door
// (T1277 / A-FABRICATE: an unresolved qualifier becomes a fabricated value
// rather than an error). So every line names a value a fabrication would
// get wrong:
//
//   line 1  the three fields the declaration writes — `skip` false, a
//           single-space grapheme, and therefore width 1. A fabricated
//           record prints width 0 or an empty grapheme.
//   line 2  the constant's own `Style`, reached THROUGH the constant. Both
//           halves false is what `Style.DEFAULT` means; a cell carrying a
//           fabricated style either panics on the field read or answers
//           `true`.
//   line 3  `Style.DEFAULT` asked directly. Its leaf name `DEFAULT` has no
//           private top-level declaration anywhere in core, so it was never
//           demoted and worked throughout. Keeping it here is what makes
//           line 2 diagnostic: if BOTH go wrong the fault is in constants
//           generally, if only line 1-2 go wrong it is this defect again.
//   line 4  `eq` against itself and against a cell that was written to, so
//           the constant is shown to be a usable value and not merely a
//           name that resolves.
mount core.term.render.cell.RenderCell;
mount core.term.style.style.Style;

fn main() {
    let e = RenderCell.EMPTY;
    print(f"empty skip={e.skip} width={e.width()} grapheme=[{e.grapheme}]");
    print(f"empty style fg={e.style.has_fg()} bg={e.style.has_bg()}");

    let d = Style.DEFAULT;
    print(f"default style fg={d.has_fg()} bg={d.has_bg()}");

    let mut other = RenderCell.EMPTY;
    other.set_char(&"X", Style.DEFAULT);
    print(f"distinct eq_self={e.eq(&e)} eq_other={e.eq(&other)}");
}
